|~ What is declared under `::builtin`, the descriptor of a
   primitive: the refusals of the kernel no reader reaches by a query,
   the table of primitives, the tree the evaluator does not know, the
   session, the printer and the sources of the root. ~|

:builtin/PayloadNotMapError
  |~~ `::builtin` holds its fields as a map, `::builtin{}` the step a
      host's verb or kind ends with; a payload of another kind is
      refused.

      ~(
        ::builtin"hello"
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::builtin/PayloadNotMapError ::string]
       )
      ~(
        ::builtin[1 2 3]
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::builtin/PayloadNotMapError ::vec]
       )
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/UnknownAstNodeTypeError
  |~~ The evaluator met a node of the parser's tree it has no rule for:
      a defect of the runtime, and no failure of the query.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/UnknownCombinatorKindError
  |~~ The evaluator met a combinator it has no rule for: a defect of the
      runtime, and no failure of the query.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/AddressBoundTwiceError
  |~~ Two files of the runtime bound an implementation under one
      address, a defect of the runtime found as it loads.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/ThrowSiteSpecAlreadyRecordedError
  |~~ Two sites of the runtime declared one refusal under one address,
      a defect of the runtime found as it loads: the address is the tag
      the refusal answers by and the name of its page, so one site would
      speak for both.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/AddressNotStringError
  |~~ A file of the runtime bound an implementation under an address
      that is no string, a defect of the runtime found as it loads.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/ImplementationNotHandedError
  |~~ A name is `::builtin{}`, or a kind ends in one, and the host
      handed no implementation for it beside its source; `:name` names
      it, and the root is refused as it is declared.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/TableSealedError
  |~~ The table of the language's implementations is sealed when the
      bootstrap completes, and one bound after it is refused.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/NumberNotFiniteLeakedToPrintError
  |~~ A number of qlang is a finite double. Source cannot mint an
      infinity or a NaN — the parser refuses the literal and every
      arithmetic site answers an error of its domain — so this tag
      reports a value a host installed. The print and the JSON of the
      boundary are where such a value shows: the print would be
      `Infinity`, which no literal reads back, and JSON would write
      `null`. `:actualValue` holds the magnitude as a string, the one
      form that prints.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/BootstrapSourceMissingError
  |~~ A source of the language resolved to nothing, so the root lacks
      what it declares; `:uri` names the source. The host maps the source
      in the imports of its package or in the import map of a browser, or
      hands the runtime a locator of its own.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/RootSourceNotDeclaredError
  |~~ A source of the root answered an error, or declared again a name
      the root holds, so its declarations stay out of the root; `:uri`
      names the source and `:tagName` the refusal, for a name declared
      again `::bind/NameDeclaredTwiceError` with `:name` the name.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/ImplementationNamesNoBuiltinError
  |~~ A host handed an implementation beside a source of the root for a
      name the source declares neither as `::builtin{}` nor as a kind
      ending in one; `:uri` names the source and `:name` the name. A
      verb runs its steps, a `::builtin{}` among them a step, so a host
      declares its primitive as a name under the label of its subject,
      `:any/@fetch ::builtin{}`, the parts of its object names under it.
      A `::builtin{}` the host hands nothing for is refused with
      `::builtin/ImplementationNotHandedError`.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/SourceLoadError
  |~~ The platform resolved a `#qlang/<ns>` logical name to a path or
      URL the host could not read. The descriptor carries `:host`
      (`:node` / `:web`), `:logicalName`, `:sourceLocation`, and either
      the underlying `:cause` or the HTTP `:status`. A host that ships
      its own catalog hands the runtime a locator of the sources of the
      language and never reaches the platform loader.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()
